  "description": "It was discovered that PyJWT incorrectly handled errors when parsing deeply\nnested token headers. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\napplications using PyJWT to fail unexpectedly, resulting in a denial of\nservice. (CVE-2026-102265)\n\nIt was discovered that PyJWT modified the options mapping supplied by an\napplication when signature verification was disabled. If an application\nreused that mapping for a later call with signature verification enabled,\nan attacker could possibly use this issue to bypass token claim checks,\nsuch as expiration. This issue only affected Ubuntu 22.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-103001)",
  "id": "USN-9212-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in PyJWT.",
